A maintainer on the project Rust-GCC/gccrs (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #3703: Performance issue with recursive macro expansion

### Summary

The compiler experiences significant performance degradation when handling deep recursive macro expansions, leading to timeouts.

### Reproducer

I tried this code:

```rust
macro_rules! fooN {
    ($cur:ident $prev:ty) => {
        #[allow(dead_code)]
        enum $cur {
            Empty,
            First($prev),
            Second($prev),
            Third($prev),
            Fourth($prev),
        }
    }
}

fooN!(Foo0 ());
fooN!(Foo1 Foo0);
fooN!(Foo2 Foo1);
fooN!(Foo3 Foo2);
fooN!(Foo4 Foo3);
