A maintainer on the project DREAM-XIN/ai-sdlc (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #272: [v0.3 prerequisite] Add trusted protected-state policy bundle materializer for #263

## Context

Issue #263 / PR #267 provides the reviewed two-anchor Vertical policy receipt/loading model. Its exact policy namespace is `config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/` on the protected `refs/heads/ai-sdlc-operator-state` ref.

Current trusted `main` Store CAS persistence is intentionally scoped to `state/operator/v1`: `RemoteGitStateRefBackend` snapshots only that Store root and `operator_store_model.is_immutable_path()` authorizes only normal Operation Store immutable/event/projection paths. It therefore cannot safely materialize PR #267's protected config policy bundle without broadening the normal Store mutation authority.

The live policy write needs a separate trusted-control materialization boundary rather than widening Worker/Store write permissions.

Current trusted main observed at issue creation: `fe1be17f4ab202b1b1be9850f5d0e2316a15834a`.

## Required outcome

Add a production-capable, trusted-control-only protected-state JSON bundle materializer that:

1. binds exact repository and protected branch ref (`refs/heads/ai-sdlc-operator-state`) from trusted configuration;
2. requires a positive `PROTECTED` `ProtectionReceipt` before any remote write;
3. accepts only exact canonical JSON files under the fixed `config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/` namespace, never arbitrary repository or normal Store paths;
4. requires exact expected remote ref SHA and performs fast-forward CAS only — no force push, no ref rewind;
5. writes one exact bundle commit parented by the expected protected-state SHA while preserving every unrelated tree path;
6. re-reads remote state immediately before push and fails on races;
7. performs a normal non-force push and then independently fetches/re-reads the durable remote commit;
8. verifies exact materialized paths and canonical JSON SHA-256 digests after the write;
9. rejects duplicate/conflicting paths, `..`, absolute paths, non-JSON paths, and namespace escape;
10. exposes the resulting exact materialization commit SHA + path/digest receipt for later `ProtectedVerticalPolicyBundleLoader` use;
11. includes deterministic real-Git validation for happy path, stale expected SHA, unprotected receipt, path escape, conflicting duplicate, remote race/non-fast-forward rejection, unrelated-state preservation, and durable digest verification;
12. does not execute live provisioning in CI or Developer work.

## Integration boundary

This materializer does **not** define the Vertical policy schemas or authority. After #267 is independently accepted/merged, Trusted-Control will construct/seal the exact Vertical rollout, writer-fence, resolution/evidence and Decision documents using the reviewed #267 authority model, then use this materializer to write them to the already protected state ref.

Do not broaden `RemoteGitStateRefBackend` normal Operation Store mutation rules just to make policy config paths writable.

## Release boundary

Completing this code/tests does not close #263 or #221. #263 closes only after trusted-main code is used for real protected policy materialization and that live materialization is independently verified. No VERSION/final release manifest changes here.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Protected-state JSON bundle materializer (OSP model of issue #272).

Models the trusted-control write path for a vertical policy bundle: a repository
anchored on a protected ref accepts an exact namespace of canonical JSON files
under a `PROTECTED` receipt, performs fast-forward CAS only, preserves unrelated
tree paths, and emits a path/digest receipt for downstream loaders.
"""

node Repo {
    has name: str = "";
    has protected_ref: str = "refs/heads/ai-sdlc-operator-state";
}

node Commit {
    has sha: str = "";
    has is_protected: bool = True;
    has expected_sha: str = "";
}

node PolicyFile {
    has path: str = "";
    has canonical_sha256: str = "";
}

node Receipt {
    has kind: str = "PLAIN";
    has namespace: str = "";
}

edge Anchors { }
edge Parents { }
edge Contains { }
edge Sealed { }

walker Materializer {
    has result_sha: str = "";
    has result_paths: list[str] = [];
    has result_digests: list[str] = [];
    has fail_reason: str = "";

    can start with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can bind_repo with Repo entry {
        print(f"binding repo={here.name} ref={here.protected_ref}");
        visit [->:Parents:->];
    }

    can audit_commit with Commit entry {
        if here.expected_sha != "" and here.expected_sha != here.sha {
            self.fail_reason = "stale expected SHA";
            disengage;
        }
        if not here.is_protected {
            self.fail_reason = "unprotected receipt";
            disengage;
        }
        visit [->:Contains:->];
    }

    can verify_files with PolicyFile entry {
        if not here.path.startswith("config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/") {
            self.fail_reason = "namespace escape";
            disengage;
        }
        if ".." in here.path or here.path.startswith("/") {
            self.fail_reason = "path traversal rejected";
            disengage;
        }
        if not here.path.endswith(".json") {
            self.fail_reason = "non-JSON path rejected";
            disengage;
        }
        for p in self.result_paths {
            if p == here.path {
                self.fail_reason = "duplicate path rejected";
                disengage;
            }
        }
        self.result_paths.append(here.path);
        self.result_digests.append(here.canonical_sha256);
        print(f"verified {here.path} sha256={here.canonical_sha256}");
    }

    can confirm_receipt with Receipt entry {
        if here.kind != "PROTECTED" {
            self.fail_reason = "receipt not PROTECTED";
            disengage;
        }
        if here.namespace != "config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/" {
            self.fail_reason = "receipt namespace mismatch";
            disengage;
        }
        self.result_sha = "f1be17ca5e7b3c0f0c2a9b1e4d6f8a7c5e3b2a10";
        print("PROTECTED receipt accepted");
    }
}

with entry {
    repo = Repo(name="dream-xin/ai-sdlc");
    protected = Commit(sha="fe1be17f4ab202b1b1be9850f5d0e2316a15834a", is_protected=True);
    rcpt = Receipt(kind="PROTECTED", namespace="config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/");
    f1 = PolicyFile(path="config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/writer-fence.json",
                    canonical_sha256="a1b2c3d4e5f6");
    f2 = PolicyFile(path="config/operator/v03-vertical-policy/resolution.json",
                    canonical_sha256="1a2b3c4d5e6f");
    unrelated_marker = PolicyFile(path="state/operator/v1/event-log.json",
                                  canonical_sha256="deadbeef0001");

    root +>:Anchors:+> repo;
    repo +>:Parents:+> protected;
    protected +>:Contains:+> f1;
    protected +>:Contains:+> f2;
    protected +>:Contains:+> unrelated_marker;
    repo +>:Sealed:+> rcpt;

    root spawn Materializer();
    m = Materializer();
    root spawn m;
    print(f"materialized_sha={m.result_sha}");
    print(f"verified_paths={m.result_paths}");
    print(f"verified_digests={m.result_digests}");
}
```

