A maintainer on the project mendi8345/agentic-qa-release-gate (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #28: Route PR Quality Map impact analysis through a dedicated Issue

## Problem proven by live smoke test

PR #27 was opened to validate the new `Quality Map Impact` gate.

The PR workflow correctly:

- created a pending `Quality Map Impact` status for the exact head SHA;
- posted one idempotent request per PR/SHA;
- ignored stale and malformed responses;
- kept the gate pending instead of accepting an unrelated Codex response.

However, when `@codex` is invoked from a pull-request conversation for a read-only impact analysis, the GitHub integration enters its normal **PR Review** mode and returns a generic review response instead of the required machine-readable Quality Map result. This occurred on both a ready PR and a Draft PR.

The same exact analysis request, when routed through this GitHub Issue, returned the required structured result for PR #27 / SHA `cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104`:

- `Map impact: NO UPDATE REQUIRED`
- `Map update state: NOT REQUIRED`
- `Merge gate: PASS`

Therefore the Quality Map decision logic works, but the Codex invocation channel must move from the PR conversation to an Issue conversation.

## Goal

Make PR-time Quality Map impact analysis complete automatically without relying on Codex custom prompts inside a PR conversation.

## Required design

1. For each PR, create or reuse one dedicated analysis Issue with a stable marker linking it to the PR number.
2. On every new PR head SHA:
   - set `Quality Map Impact` to pending on the exact SHA;
   - post exactly one `@codex` analysis request for that PR/SHA in the dedicated Issue;
   - include the PR URL, PR number, exact head SHA, required headings, and exact machine-readable contract.
3. On bot responses in that Issue:
   - accept only `chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]`;
   - require the exact schema from Issue #25;
   - resolve the linked PR number from a trusted issue marker;
   - re-fetch the PR and verify the response SHA equals the current remote PR head;
   - set success only for a valid PASS decision;
   - set failure for a valid BLOCK decision or malformed authoritative response;
   - ignore stale-SHA responses.
4. Reuse the same dedicated Issue for subsequent SHAs of the same PR, while preserving one request per exact PR/SHA.
5. Keep privileged workflows read-only with respect to PR-controlled code. Use GitHub API reads only.
6. Do not accept the generic `Codex Review` response as a Quality Map result.
7. Keep PR #27 open as the live smoke-test fixture until the corrected flow reaches PASS. Do not merge the smoke-test PR.

## Deterministic validation

Add tests for:

- creating/reusing the dedicated analysis Issue;
- exact PR/SHA request idempotency;
- trusted issue marker parsing;
- bot-only response acceptance;
- current-SHA PASS;
- current-SHA BLOCK;
- stale SHA ignored;
- malformed response blocked;
- generic `Codex Review` ignored;
- a new PR head creates a new request in the same analysis Issue;
- no duplicate request for the same PR/SHA.

## Acceptance criteria

- PR #27 receives a successful `Quality Map Impact` status for its current exact head through the Issue-routed analysis flow.
- Existing CI remains green.
- The PR remains unmerged after the smoke test.
- The dedicated analysis Issue provides a durable audit trail for every analyzed PR SHA.

<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:27 -->

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""PR Quality Map impact analysis routing — Issue-channel model.

Models the core scenario from Issue #28: a PR's Quality Map impact analysis
must be routed through a dedicated GitHub Issue rather than the PR
conversation, so the bot returns the machine-readable schema instead of
a generic PR Review response. Nodes represent the PR, the dedicated
analysis Issue, the bot responses, and the requested SHAs. A walker
walks the Issue-threaded audit trail to verify routing invariants.
"""

node Repo {
    has name: str = "";
}

node PullRequest {
    has number: int = 0;
    has head_sha: str = "";
    has title: str = "";
    has gate_state: str = "pending";
    has status_sha: str = "";
    has last_decision: str = "";
    has merged: bool = False;
}

edge AnalysisIssue {
    has marker: str = "";
}

edge CodexRequest {
    has posted_sha: str = "";
}

node AnalysisThread {
    has issue_number: int = 0;
    has pr_number: int = 0;
    has marker: str = "";
    has request_count: int = 0;
}

node CodexResponse {
    has author: str = "";
    has schema: str = "";
    has response_sha: str = "";
    has decision: str = "";
    has trusted_marker: str = "";
}

edge PostedTo {
    has request_sha: str = "";
}

edge RepliedWith {
    has bot_login: str = "";
}

walker ImpactAuditor {
    has accepted: int = 0;
    has rejected: int = 0;
    has stale: int = 0;
    has generic_review: int = 0;
    has trusted_only: bool = True;

    can begin with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can scan_repo with Repo entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can scan_pr with PullRequest entry {
        print(f"PR #{here.number} head={here.head_sha} gate={here.gate_state} decision={here.last_decision}");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can scan_thread with AnalysisThread entry {
        expected = f"<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:{here.pr_number} -->";
        if here.marker != expected {
            self.trusted_only = False;
            print(f"  THREAD marker mismatch: {here.marker}");
        } else {
            print(f"  THREAD #{here.issue_number} trusted marker ok; requests={here.request_count}");
        }
        visit [-->];
    }

    can scan_response with CodexResponse entry {
        trusted_marker = f"<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:";
        if here.author != "chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]" {
            self.rejected += 1;
            print(f"  REJECT non-bot author={here.author}");
        } elif here.schema == "Codex Review" {
            self.generic_review += 1;
            print(f"  REJECT generic Codex Review");
        } elif here.schema != "Quality Map" {
            self.rejected += 1;
            print(f"  REJECT unknown schema={here.schema}");
        } elif here.trusted_marker == "" {
            self.rejected += 1;
            print(f"  REJECT missing trusted marker");
        } else {
            self.accepted += 1;
            print(f"  ACCEPT decision={here.decision} sha={here.response_sha}");
        }
        visit [-->];
    }
}

with entry {
    repo = Repo(name="agentic-qa-release-gate");
    pr27 = PullRequest(number=27, head_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104",
                       title="Quality Map Impact gate (smoke)", gate_state="pending",
                       status_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104",
                       last_decision="PASS", merged=False);
    pr_new = PullRequest(number=28, head_sha="aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111",
                         title="Second PR", gate_state="pending",
                         status_sha="aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111",
                         last_decision="PASS", merged=False);

    marker27 = "<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:27 -->";
    marker_new = "<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:28 -->";

    thread27 = AnalysisThread(issue_number=101, pr_number=27, marker=marker27, request_count=2);
    thread_new = AnalysisThread(issue_number=102, pr_number=28, marker=marker_new, request_count=1);

    root ++> repo
        ++> pr27
        ++> pr_new;

    pr27 +>:AnalysisIssue(marker=marker27):+> thread27;
    pr_new +>:AnalysisIssue(marker=marker_new):+> thread_new;

    valid_marker27 = "<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:27 -->";
    valid_marker_new = "<!-- quality-map-pr-impact-routing-fix smoke-pr:28 -->";

    thread27 +>:CodexRequest(posted_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104"):+>
        CodexResponse(author="chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]", schema="Quality Map",
                      response_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104",
                      decision="PASS", trusted_marker=valid_marker27);

    thread27 +>:CodexRequest(posted_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104"):+>
        CodexResponse(author="chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]", schema="Quality Map",
                      response_sha="0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
                      decision="BLOCK", trusted_marker=valid_marker27);

    thread27 +>:CodexRequest(posted_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104"):+>
        CodexResponse(author="chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]", schema="Codex Review",
                      response_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104",
                      decision="", trusted_marker="");

    thread27 +>:CodexRequest(posted_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104"):+>
        CodexResponse(author="random-user", schema="Quality Map",
                      response_sha="cccff1fab7b0ee8982806d71f8a3a128c14c4104",
                      decision="PASS", trusted_marker=valid_marker27);

    thread_new +>:CodexRequest(posted_sha="aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111"):+>
        CodexResponse(author="chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]", schema="Quality Map",
                      response_sha="aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111",
                      decision="PASS", trusted_marker=valid_marker_new);

    print("Routing audit (Issue-channel model):");
    root spawn ImpactAuditor();
    audit = ImpactAuditor();
    print(f"summary accepted={audit.accepted} rejected={audit.rejected} "
          f"generic_review={audit.generic_review} trusted_marker_ok={audit.trusted_only}");
    print(f"PR #27 merged={pr27.merged} gate={pr27.gate_state}");
}
```

